`,s.jsxs(e.p,{children:["A control engineer can only control what they can ",s.jsx(e.strong,{children:"predict"}),'. Before we ask "how fast does this system respond?" or "does it oscillate?", we need a mathematical model of the physical thing — a transfer function, or at least a differential equation. This module shows how to get that model for ',s.jsx(e.strong,{children:"electrical circuits"}),", the most common building blocks of sensors, filters, amplifiers and motor drives."]}),`
`,s.jsx(e.p,{children:'Start with something concrete. You close a switch and a battery starts charging a capacitor through a resistor (think of the flash of an old camera, or the "power-on" delay of a device). Questions you might ask:'}),`
